+ ### Detection API Calls (Per Tool Call)
+ **What happens on each agent tool call:**
+ 1. **Agent executes tool** (e.g., `bash`, `read_file`, `web_fetch`)
+ 2. **MoltGuard intercepts** (before execution)
+    - Sanitizes tool parameters locally
+    - Replaces secrets/PII with placeholders
+ 3. **Detection API call**
+    - **Endpoint:** `POST https://www.openguardrails.com/core/api/v1/detect`
+    - **Headers:**
+      Content-Type: application/json
+      X-API-Key: sk-og-abc123...
+    - **Payload sent (example):**
+        "agentId": "agent_xyz789...",
+        "agentId": "agent_xyz789...",
+        "tool": "bash",
+        "parameters": {
+          "command": "curl <URL> -H 'Authorization: Bearer <SECRET>'"
+        },
+        "agentIntent": "Fetch user data from API",
+        "timestamp": "2026-03-05T10:30:00Z"
+          "classification": "safe",
+          "confidence": 0.95,
+          "scanners": [
+            {"id": "S01", "result": "safe"},
+            {"id": "S08", "result": "safe"}
+          ],
+          "quotaRemaining": 499
+ 4. **MoltGuard decision**
+    - `safe` → Allow tool execution
+    - `suspicious` → Warn user, allow with caution
+    - `blocked` → Block tool execution, notify user
+ 5. **Tool executes** (if allowed)
+ **To verify detection API calls:**
+ # Monitor detection calls
+ sudo tcpdump -i any -w detection.pcap -s 0 -A host openguardrails.com
+ # Trigger a tool call (read a file)
+ tcpdump -r detection.pcap -A | grep -A 30 "POST /api/v1/detect"
+ # CRITICAL: Verify no unsanitized secrets
+ grep -i "sk-ant\|sk-proj\|password\|@.*\.com" detection.pcap
+ # Expected: No raw secrets (should only see <SECRET>, <EMAIL>, etc.)
